description "Login policy: faillock lockout, password quality, rescue sulogin"

supports "fedora" "debian" "ubuntu"

// On a deb family the two config files this module ships are inert until
// something puts the modules that read them in the stack, which is what
// `deb/files/usr/share/pam-configs/` and `deb/finalize.sh` do. `cracklib-runtime`
// is not optional there: `dictcheck = 1` without a dictionary fails **every**
// password change rather than falling back.
family "debian" "ubuntu" {
    packages "libpam-pwquality" "cracklib-runtime"
}

// This module shipped `disable sshd.service` in a preset until 2026-09-07 and
// no longer does, because it was a posture rather than a claim and it collided
// with the module that owns the question. **It backed nothing measured**:
// `service_sshd_disabled` scans `notapplicable` under `cusp_fedora`, and every
// `satisfies` below is faillock or pwquality. Meanwhile `login-access` exists
// to say that neither a base nor a hardening default should decide whether a
// machine is reachable, and it enables the same unit.
//
// Both landed in the fedora collection image on 2026-09-07 and contradicted
// each other. `finalize.sh` applies presets as `systemctl enable`/`disable` per
// line in glob order, so **the last file wins** — the two are `45-module-login-
// access` and `45-module-login-policy`, and the disable took it on nothing but
// the alphabet. It surfaced only because `validate-image` checks that an
// `enable` took effect and does not check the other direction: sorted the
// other way, this line would have lost in silence.
//
// So ssh is `login-access`'s to decide, and an image wanting the old behaviour
// declines to import it rather than importing two modules that disagree.

// The claim is Fedora's alone because a benchmark number is not portable
// across families. Measured 2026-09-07: `ssg-debian13-ds.xml` and
// `ssg-ubuntu2404-ds.xml` carry no CCI number and no `AC-7.1(ii)` -- DISA is
// written as `SRG-OS-…` there -- so all four name nothing on a deb scan. The
// faillock and pwquality rules those datastreams do carry are claimed once the
// deb hardening leg has measured this image against them, not before.
family "fedora" {
    satisfies {
        stig "CCI-001619" \
            "CCI-000194" \
            "CCI-000195"
        nist "AC-7.1(ii)"
    }
}
